{title: I won’t turn back}
{x_theme: faith-trust, victory}
{x_source: docx:1. Incomplete/I won_t turn back.docx}

{comment: Chorus}
The mountain is high, but it’s not too steep
The battle is rough but I’m not too weak
And I won’t turn back, no, I won’t turn back
The road is hard, but it’s not too long
The enemy’s near but he’s not too strong
And I won’t turn back, no, I won’t turn back

{comment: Bridge}
Though the enemy bring war against my soul
Though an host of evil battles for control
I will not fear for the Lord, He is near
And His angels encamp all around me

{comment: Verse 1}
It’s a struggle for survival, we daily meet the foe
We’re out here on the battle field, there’s times be stand alone
That’s when I reach for my Holy armor, take out my shield of faith
I march onto that battlefield, take out my sword and say

{comment: Verse 2}
In the face of persecution, we press on through the night
For often on that battlefield we walk by faith and not by sight
We march through persecution, determined come what may
We have to fight the good fight, we have to keep the faith
